{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VNzsxgdPpHaXm1WJagLp2e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze the project context carefully and propose tasks according to the constraints.\n\n## Step 1: Analyze Project Context\n\nThis is a Go project that re-implements Unix utilities from specifications derived from C source code. The pipeline is: extract → specify → synthesize → verify.\n\n## Step 2: Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specs. Re-implementations diverge from reference behavior on edge cases.\n\n**Architecture**:\n- `cmd/` - per-utility Go implementations\n- `pkg/testutils/` - differential testing harness\n- `pkg/sys/` - syscall abstractions (Darwin/Linux)\n\n\n- `pkg/format/` - output formatting (columns, colors, sizes)\n- `magefiles/` - build targets\n- `docs/` - specifications\n\n**Current Implementation State**: Looking at the existing codebase, I can see that the differential testing harness, syscall abstractions, and formatting utilities are already in place. The `cat` and `wc` commands have been implemented with their test suites, though the listing appears to cut off mid-implementation.\n\n**Release Timeline**: The foundational packages are marked as specification-complete but not yet started, while the individual command implementations like `wc`, `cat`, `sponge`, and `du` are also specification-complete and awaiting development.\n\n**Discrepancy Check**: The analysis metadata says \"not started,\" but the source code clearly shows implementations already exist for these packages. Following the constraint to trust the actual source code over documentation descriptions, I need to reconcile what's really there versus what the status claims.\n\n**Actual Implementation Status**: Looking at what's present in the codebase, the core packages have substantial implementations with test coverage already in place—`testutils`, `sys`, and `format` all have their main files and corresponding test files implemented.\n\n**Critical Gap Identified**: The `cmd/du/` directory has a `main.go` implementation but is missing its test file (`du_test.go`), which breaks the pattern of complete test coverage that exists for all the other command implementations.\n\nNow I'm checking which releases these commands belong to and what the constraints are on proposing tasks. The scope limits me to releases 00.0 through 01.3, and I can only suggest one task maximum. Let me verify the status across each release to identify what's actually missing.\n\nGoing through the releases systematically, I can see that most packages and commands have both code and tests in place. But when I look at rel01.3 for the du command, I notice the source code listing includes `cmd/du/main.go` but is missing `cmd/du/du_test.go`. That's the gap—the differential tests for du aren't documented in the source code section. I should track down the PRD and test suite for du to properly anchor this task.\n\nLooking at the du implementation, it covers the main requirements from prd009-du: directory traversal with size accumulation, various output flags like `-h` and `--apparent-size`, hard-link deduplication, and proper signal and error handling. I can see from the existing test files in other commands that they follow a consistent pattern—they build the Go binary, locate the reference implementation, and then run individual test cases. I need to apply that same structure to create the missing du test file. I'm realizing that du's output depends on actual filesystem block allocation, which varies across systems, but the differential testing approach handles this since both binaries run on the same filesystem. I need to structure the du_test.go file following the patterns from other test files, keeping it under 250 lines with a single task anchored to the PRD requirements.\n\nThe test should cover default behavior with various paths, flag combinations like -h, -s, -a, -b, -c, and -d, hard-link deduplication, and error handling for missing paths. I'll need to reference the du implementation, the differential test harness, similar test patterns from wc and cat, and the specific requirements from prd009-du.\n\nNow I'm examining the main.go implementation to map out which requirements need coverage. The default traversal behavior needs differential tests for depth-first ordering and current directory defaults, while the flags require separate test groupings since I can only cover four requirements per task. I'll start with R1 for default traversal behavior and then structure the remaining flag and error handling tests accordingly.\n\nFor the design approach, I'm following the established patterns from other command tests by using the differential testing framework with gdu as the reference binary, and I'll need to construct temporary directory structures to validate the behavior against the reference implementation. I'm reading through the task structure now. The use case rel01.3-uc001-du covers both the specification and the differential test, so I need to create du_test.go following the same pattern as wc_test.go and cat_test.go. Based on the complexity of the du command and comparing line counts from similar test files, I'm estimating this will be around 150-250 lines covering the core flags and edge cases.\n\nLooking at the PRD references in main.go, I can see du has R1 through R5, with R4.2 handling error cases. I'll organize the test requirements into four groups: R1 for default traversal and size reporting, R2 for display and depth flags, R3 for hard-link deduplication, and R4 for error handling. Now I'm ready to write the test file with the title \"prd009-du R1, R2, R3, R4 -- differential tests for cmd/du\".","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":79769,"cache_read_input_tokens":19292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":79769},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"226d1c85-b000-4ac3-835e-45e4046bec8e","uuid":"99202027-9da7-4bb8-8ed5-65be0b726175"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VNzsxgdPpHaXm1WJagLp2e","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specs accessible to implementers. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies parity through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). `cmd/` holds per-utility Go implementations, `pkg/testutils/` provides the differential testing harness, `pkg/sys/` wraps platform syscalls, `pkg/format/` handles shared output formatting. `magefiles/` bridges human-guided spec work and automated code generation.\n\n**Current State**: Source code exists for `pkg/testutils`, `pkg/sys`, `pkg/format`, `cmd/version`, `cmd/wc`, `cmd/cat`, `cmd/sponge`, and `cmd/du`. All packages have both implementation and test files **except** `cmd/du` which has `main.go` but no `du_test.go`.\n\n**Current Release**: Releases 00.0 through 01.2 appear complete (code + tests exist). Release 01.3 (`cmd/du`) has implementation but is missing its differential test file.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nThe earliest incomplete release is **rel01.3** (du). The implementation exists (`cmd/du/main.go`, 228 lines covering prd009-du R1-R5), but the differential test file `cmd/du/du_test.go` does not exist in the source tree. All dependencies are satisfied: `pkg/testutils` (the harness), `pkg/sys` (used by du for `Lstat`), and `pkg/format` (used by du for `HumanSize`) all exist with tests. The single remaining deliverable is the test file.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"prd009-du R1, R2, R3, R4 -- differential tests for cmd/du\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - cmd/du/main.go (implementation under test -- covers prd009-du R1, R2, R3, R4, R5)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests harness)\n      - cmd/wc/wc_test.go (reference pattern for differential test file structure)\n      - cmd/cat/cat_test.go (reference pattern for TestMain, writeFile helpers)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd009-du.yaml (requirements being tested)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel01.3.yaml (test suite specification for du)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/du/du_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Differential tests comparing Go du binary against GNU gdu reference\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: |\n          Write differential tests for default traversal and size reporting\n          (prd009-du R1.1 default to current directory, R1.3 depth-first output\n          order, R1.4 child accumulation, R1.5 non-directory argument). Tests must\n          create temporary directory trees with known file content and compare Go\n          binary output against gdu reference binary using testutils.RunDiffTests.\n      - id: R2\n        text: |\n          Write differential tests for display and depth flags (prd009-du R2.1\n          human-readable -h, R2.2 summarize -s, R2.5 -k accepted, R2.7 grand\n          total -c, R2.8 apparent-size). Each flag and flag combination must have\n          at least one DiffTest case exercising it.\n      - id: R3\n        text: |\n          Write differential tests for hard-link deduplication (prd009-du R3.1\n          dev+ino tracking, R3.2 nlink > 1 files counted once, R3.3 directories\n          excluded from dedup). Tests must create hard links in a temp directory\n          and verify both binaries produce identical totals.\n      - id: R4\n        text: |\n          Write differential tests for error handling and exit codes (prd009-du\n          R4.2 stderr format for missing paths, R5.1 SIGPIPE handler does not\n          cause nonzero exit). Include tests for nonexistent paths and mixed\n          valid/invalid arguments.\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: |\n          Follow the TestMain pattern from cmd/wc/wc_test.go and cmd/cat/cat_test.go:\n          locate reference binary via exec.LookPath(\"gdu\"), build Go binary to a\n          temp directory via \"go build -o <path> .\", store paths in package-level\n          goBinaryPath and refBinaryPath variables, clean up in deferred os.RemoveAll.\n          Skip all tests with os.Exit(0) if gdu is not found.\n      - id: D2\n        text: |\n          Use testutils.DiffTest and testutils.RunDiffTests for all test cases.\n          du writes to stdout (not to files), so the standard harness is sufficient\n          without the custom fileDiffTest infrastructure used by sponge. Set WorkDir\n          to a temp directory containing the test file tree for each test group.\n      - id: D3\n        text: |\n          Create temporary directory trees with known file content using os.MkdirTemp,\n          os.Mkdir, os.WriteFile, and os.Link (for hard-link tests). Use a writeFile\n          helper consistent with the pattern in cmd/cat/cat_test.go and cmd/wc/wc_test.go.\n          Temp directories are managed by t.TempDir() for automatic cleanup.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: cmd/du/du_test.go exists and compiles with \"go build ./cmd/du/\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/du/ runs without build errors (tests may skip if gdu is not installed)\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: |\n          Test file contains at least 12 DiffTest cases covering: default directory\n          traversal, -h flag, -s flag, -c flag, -a flag, -d flag, -b flag, -k flag,\n          hard-link deduplication, nonexistent path error, mixed valid/invalid paths,\n          and empty directory.\n      - id: AC4\n        text: |\n          Every test function has a comment referencing the prd009-du requirement IDs\n          it exercises, matching the pattern in cmd/cat/cat_test.go (e.g.,\n          \"// --- Default traversal (prd009-du R1.1, R1.3) ---\").\n      - id: AC5\n        text: |\n          File header comment includes copyright, SPDX license, package doc with\n          Implements and Traces lines matching the pattern:\n          \"// Implements: prd009-du R1, R2, R3, R4, R5\"\n          \"// Traces: test-rel01.3, rel01.3-uc001-du\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":79769,"cache_read_input_tokens":19292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":79769},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"226d1c85-b000-4ac3-835e-45e4046bec8e","uuid":"ec90c07e-0040-4977-a656-78be2aa405fe"}
